#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/introduction/warm-up/unsafe-trait.md:22
msgid ""
"“If the requirements of the trait are semantic, then your trait may not need "
"any methods at all. The documentation is essential, however.”"
msgstr ""

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/introduction/warm-up/unsafe-trait.md:25
msgid ""
"“Traits without methods are called marker traits. When implementing them for "
"types, you are adding information to the type system. You have now given the "
"compiler the ability to talk about types that meet the requirements "
"described in the documentation.”"
msgstr ""
